  "steps": [
    "Heat 2 tablespoons of the olive oil in a large wide pan over medium-high heat. Add the aubergine and cook for 6 to 8 minutes, stirring occasionally, until lightly browned and starting to soften. Remove to a plate.",
    "Add the remaining oil to the pan, then cook the onion and peppers for 5 minutes until the onion is translucent and the peppers are beginning to soften. Add the garlic and cook for 30 seconds more.",
    "Stir in the courgette and cook for 3 minutes, then add the tomato paste, canned tomatoes, water, oregano, thyme, bay leaf, salt and black pepper.",
    "Return the aubergine to the pan, bring to a gentle simmer, then lower the heat and cook uncovered for 25 to 30 minutes, stirring now and then, until the vegetables are tender and the sauce is thick and glossy.",
    "Remove the bay leaf, taste and adjust the seasoning. Stir through the basil just before serving."
  ],
